<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n72195" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἴαξ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾱκος</span>, 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἴηξ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ηκος</span>, ὁ, prop. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>handle of rudder, tiller</i> (<i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				1.89
			</span></i>), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πηδαλίων οἴακος
			ἀφέμενος</span> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πηδάλιον</span>)
				<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Plt.</u>
				272e
			</span></i> : generally, <i>helm,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἴακος εὐθυντῆρος ὑστάτου νεώς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					717
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρέφειν οἴακα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hel.</u>
					1591
				</span></i>
			 : pl., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰάκων φύλαξ</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				1578
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἴακες εὐπρύμνου νεώς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>IT</u>
					1357
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν οἴακα εἴσω ἄγειν ἢ ἔξω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Alc.</u>
					1.117c
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph.,
				<i>helm of government,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν πρύμνῃ πόλεως οἴ. νωμῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Th.</u>
					3
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πραπίδων οἴ. νέμων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					802
				</span></i>
			 (anap.) ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαλινῶν ἔργον οἰάκων θ᾽ ἅμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					869
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Or.</u>
				795
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν οἴ. στρέφει δαίμων ἑκάστῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Anaxandr.
					4
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τύχης οἴ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					7.3226.5
				</span></i>
			 (Orchom. 
				Boeot.
			) ; 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡροσκόπος</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Paul.Al.
				<u>L.</u>
				2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				24.269
			</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἴηκες</span> are prob.
				<i>rings of the yoke,</i> through which pass the reins for
			guiding the mules, cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕστωρ.</span></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
